// src/v4/compiler/05_emit.dag
//
// Scope: target-source projection from the inferred tree and a target
//        model — the U1 Realize phase, the structural inverse of
//        `ingest`. Per-target specialization (T-11) and the full-stack
//        omni-emission demo contract (T-16) are owned here: emit is the
//        single coercion=emission authority (STRUCTURE.md §"coercion =
//        emission"). There is no parallel per-target emitter and no
//        separate omni-projection mechanism.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_generation_(compiler)
//
// ── WAVE-0 SCOPE (interface-freeze + witness/Acceptance design layer) ──
//
//   This is the bounded Wave-0 deliverable for T-11 + T-16: the
//   immutable I/O contract, the per-target / omni design contract, and
//   the worked Acceptance examples a Wave-3+ worker must satisfy. It is
//   NOT the implementation. Per the anti-conflation rule (codex BLOCKING
//   `a67577c3`): Wave-0 ≠ dependency-satisfied implementation. No carrier
//   is minted here; the real per-target grammar-data fold and the omni
//   projection are the NAMED Wave-3 triggers below, not this PR.
//
//   NAMED REFINE TRIGGERS (explicit — refine-to-real is Wave-3+, NOT here):
//     • T-11 real fill — TRIGGER: T-10 orchestrator real (`emit ∘ core ∘
//       ingest` over a real `InferredTree`) + T-4 ×5 Shape-A language
//       models grammar-as-data landed. Wave-4 IMPL per TASKS.md T-11.
//     • T-16 real fill — TRIGGER: T-11 real + T-4.5–T-4.8 (coordination /
//       react / formats) landed. Wave-5 IMPL per TASKS.md T-16.
//
//   WITNESSES OFF REFINEMENT (Wave-0 discipline, operator-pinned): the
//   Acceptance design below does NOT use refinement keys or
//   `NonEmptyList`. Those are deferred to `std/collection.dag` Wave-A2 /
//   T-25-core (a refined `List<T> where non_empty`, never a per-file
//   mint — 5-language precedent, operator-flagged). Any Acceptance shape
//   that would need a non-empty/refined carrier is held until T-25-core
//   lands OR is named as an explicit Wave-3 trigger above. Do NOT mint a
//   local refinement to make a witness expressible — STOP and escalate.
//
// ── NO-TEMPLATING CONSTRAINT (operator 2026-05-17, binding) ──
//
//   emit goes THROUGH the grounded target model's grammar-as-data, run
//   in the inverse direction — NEVER a string template or print routine.
//   The declarative bidirectional grammar relation (concrete-syntax ⟷
//   `Node`) is authored once (T-4 / T-7) and consumed in BOTH directions:
//   forward = parse (T-7), inverse = emit. A string-templated emit path
//   is the emit-side D2 hollow alias — an artifact the compiler cannot
//   ground and coercion-check. The per-target "translation tables" of
//   T-11 ARE this grammar-as-data, NOT fill-in-the-holes templates. STOP
//   if any emission step cannot be expressed as the inverse grammar walk.
//
// ── T-11: PER-TARGET SPECIALIZATION (×5 Shape-A) ──
//
//   The five Shape-A targets — rust / python / go / cpp / typescript —
//   match T-4's language set and the execution-graph critical path; T-16
//   depends on the full set. Per-target behavior is the inverse walk of
//   each target's own grammar-as-data model (`extdeps/languages/<t>`),
//   never an `if target == X` special-case in emit. Per STRUCTURE.md:
//   "every emitter special case is evidence of an ungrounded concept
//   upstream" — a special-case in this file is a STOP signal pointing at
//   a missing fact in `04_infer.dag` (owns) or the target's language
//   model, not a local branch to add here.
//
//   Target-specific optimization (or its principled absence) is a
//   cost-lens-derived realization decision (U1/U2 cost spine, per-target
//   from `extdeps/languages/<t>`), taken at this emit boundary — it is
//   read, never a heuristic guess. Same `InferredTree` → five
//   cost-derived realizations; the model never changes, only the
//   per-target realize step does (mirrors lens/parallelism.dag example C).
//
// ── T-16: FULL-STACK OMNI-EMISSION DEMO CONTRACT ──
//
//   ONE `.dag` program → a multi-language, multi-endpoint application.
//   The structural guarantee is gate #28 `omni_layers_share_one_node_
//   tree`: all projected artifacts share ONE `Node` tree — coherence is
//   STRUCTURAL, not test-checked. The N-target projection set (gate #28
//   is layer-count-agnostic; canvas Q4 EXTEND, NOT a parallel gate —
//   INVARIANTS P1):
//     • Rust backend            — Shape-A (existing language model)
//     • C++ backend (variant)   — Shape-A
//     • TypeScript + React UI   — Shape-A (canvas Q2-a: a React component
//                                 IS TS source at emit time; Q5-a:
//                                 `Component` is `Behavior::Bind`, no new
//                                 substrate kind)
//     • OpenAPI wire contract   — Shape-B (`extdeps/formats/openapi.dag`)
//     • SQL DDL persistence     — Shape-B (canvas #4 fork (a): emitted
//                                 THROUGH a grounded ISO-SQL format
//                                 model so the schema is coercion-
//                                 checked — never a string DDL printout.
//                                 That model is `extdeps/formats/
//                                 sql.dag`, a NOT-YET-LANDED T-4.6
//                                 formats-bundle extension; this layer
//                                 does NOT freeze a Consumes edge to it
//                                 — see the named pending dependency
//                                 below)
//     • Markdown docs           — Shape-B
//
//   Endpoint partitioning (which program fragment runs where) is
//   expressed via `extdeps/coordination.dag`'s `Endpoint` /
//   `DeploymentUnit`; the cross-endpoint wire contract derives from the
//   shared domain types (one `Node` tree ⇒ Rust and TypeScript carry the
//   SAME domain types by construction). Cross-target consistency is
//   therefore structural here and L5-tested downstream, not re-asserted
//   by a parallel mechanism in this file.
//
// ── WORKED ACCEPTANCE (design contract — Wave-3+ worker fills to satisfy;
//     refinement-free per the Wave-0 discipline above) ──
//
//   A. Inverse-grammar emit (T-11, golden). A typed `InferredTree` node
//      for a record + a target language model → that target's concrete
//      syntax, produced by the INVERSE walk of the target's grammar-as-
//      data. Round-trips: `parse(emit(n, t)) == n` for every Shape-A `t`
//      (the bidirectional relation authored once, consumed both ways).
//
//   B. Fail-closed on un-emittable (T-11, Diagnostic path). A node whose
//      concept has no grounded production in target `t`'s grammar model
//      → a precise `Diagnostic` (which concept, which target, which
//      missing production) — NEVER a fabricated or templated string.
//      The architecture refusing to lie is the demonstrable result.
//
//   C. Same tree, five realizations (T-11). One `InferredTree` →
//      rust/python/go/cpp/typescript artifacts, each the inverse walk of
//      its own grammar model; differences are cost-realize-derived and
//      inspectable per target, never an emit special-case.
//
//   D. ONE Node tree, N projections (T-16, gate #28). One omni `.dag`
//      program → {Rust, TS+React, OpenAPI, SQL DDL, Markdown}, all read
//      off the SAME `Node` tree. The Rust and TS domain types are
//      structurally the same node — wire-contract derivation needs no
//      separate declaration; divergence is impossible by construction,
//      not caught by a test.
//
//   E. Endpoint partition coherence (T-16). A `DeploymentUnit` over two
//      `Endpoint`s (backend Rust + frontend TS/React) → each fragment
//      emits for its endpoint's language; the `WireContract` between
//      them is the shared-type projection, fail-closed if the two
//      endpoints' views of a domain type diverge (they cannot, given
//      gate #28 — this Acceptance proves the impossibility is structural).
//
// I/O — Owns (immutable contract; SINGLE temporal authority — the
//   pending CP-1b / `00_compile.dag` train, not "already merged Owns"):
//
//   `Result<…, Diagnostic>` below is the TASKS / orchestrator-target
//   spelling that `00_compile.dag` / `05_emit.dag` `Owns` will carry
//   once the CP-1b / `00_compile.dag` train (incl. the
//   TargetSpec↔TargetModel freeze) freezes it. It is NOT yet grounded
//   in merged `Owns`: at HEAD both files are bare scaffolds (`Owns:
//   none.`), and the landed fail-closed carrier in `std/diagnostic.dag`
//   is `Outcome<T>` (DECISIONS.md item I) — there is no `Result<ok,err>`
//   `.dag` type today. One authority, one tense: this header states the
//   forward contract the train will land; it does NOT claim `Result`
//   already lives in merged `Owns` or in `diagnostic.dag`. Do NOT
//   standardize the spelling to `Outcome<…>` independently — the
//   spelling is settled with `00_compile.dag` in that same train, not
//   here.
//
//   - emit: (InferredTree, TargetModel) -> Result<TargetSource, Diagnostic>
//       the emit boundary / U1 Realize phase; structural inverse of
//       `ingest`; the single per-target (T-11) and omni (T-16) authority.
//   - compile: (Source, TargetModel) -> Result<TargetSource, Diagnostic>
//       the orchestrator, `emit ∘ core ∘ ingest` (T-10-owned composition;
//       referenced here only for the literal `Owns` alignment).
//
// Consumes (closed; reference only — no new files, substrate extension =
//   STOP signal):
//   - std/node.dag           — the universal `Node` IR (gate #28: ONE tree)
//   - std/diagnostic.dag     — fail-closed branch carrier (`Outcome<T>`
//                              today, DECISIONS.md item I; the `Result`
//                              spelling is the pending-train forward
//                              contract — see the single-temporal-
//                              authority note in the I/O block above)
//   - extdeps/languages/{rust,python,go,cpp,typescript}.dag
//                            — the ×5 Shape-A grammar-as-data models
//                              (inverse walk = emit; never a template)
//   - extdeps/formats/openapi.dag       — T-16 Shape-B wire-contract
//                              projection (coercion-checked, not printed)
//
//   Named pending dependency (NOT a frozen closed-tree Consumes edge —
//   the file is not on `main`; INVARIANTS P2):
//   - extdeps/formats/sql.dag — T-16 Shape-B SQL-DDL persistence
//                              projection. NOT-YET-LANDED: scheduled as
//                              the T-4.6 formats-bundle 7th-file
//                              extension (canvas #4 fork (a)). The T-16
//                              real-fill trigger above already gates on
//                              T-4.6; the SQL projection binds when
//                              `sql.dag` lands, not before.
//   - extdeps/frameworks/react.dag      — T-16 React-as-TS (canvas Q2-a)
//   - extdeps/coordination.dag          — T-16 endpoint partitioning
//                              (`Endpoint` / `DeploymentUnit` /
//                              `WireContract`)
//
// Dissolution disposition (Practice 4): 🟢 — no dissolution work. This
//   PR authors the interface-freeze + Acceptance design layer ONLY; it
//   mints NO carrier, no walker, no emit-template, no refinement. There
//   is therefore no dissolution-class surface in the diff and no
//   downstream dissolve named here. Carrier impl + witnesses are the
//   NAMED Wave-3 triggers above (TASKS.md T-11 / T-16), not deferred
//   prose.
//
